<http://data.silknow.org/object/1095464d-6226-3809-ad1d-638c17ff0521>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Enclosed in 1975.437.3a, b, a carved and polychromed vitrine. This type of figure, called \"Bräutigam-Typus\", was made for nuns upon profession of vows and becoming \"bride of Christ.\" See 24.80.92 for another example of this type. The devotional emblem (d) can be read as follows: cross = faith, flaming heart = devotion, anchor = hope."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/572b522b-8bf4-300a-9af1-89bed6d1cceb> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/fc08f965-6f2e-3a4d-8edd-d1db6dd368eb> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/c0ce5eae-dfeb-3f3e-89c2-0ed7b7310435> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Enclosed in 1975.437.3a, b, a carved and polychromed vitrine. This type of figure, called \"Bräutigam-Typus\", was made for nuns upon profession of vows and becoming \"bride of Christ.\" See 24.80.92 for another example of this type. The devotional emblem (d) can be read as follows: cross = faith, flaming heart = devotion, anchor = hope."@en ;
        dc:identifier                  "1975.437.4a–e" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/206372> .

